Title:
Custom PowerShell Runspace in C# with AMSI Bypass, ETW Blinding, and Full Language Mode

Type:
Blog Post

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- The post describes a C# console tool that hosts the PowerShell engine in a custom runspace while neutralizing AMSI scanning and PowerShell ETW telemetry.  
- It targets common post-exploitation friction points where PowerShell payloads are blocked by AMSI or heavily logged via ETW/script block logging.  
- The core techniques use .NET reflection to flip internal PowerShell flags (`AmsiUtils.amsiInitFailed` and `EtwActivity.isEtwEnabled`) rather than patching `amsi.dll`, reducing reliance on noisy native API calls.  
- It also forces `PSLanguageMode.FullLanguage` inside the hosted runspace to sidestep Constrained Language Mode typically enforced on `powershell.exe` via WDAC/AppLocker.  
- Useful for red teams/pentesters building custom PowerShell hosts and for blue teams understanding how telemetry can be suppressed and where to detect (non-standard processes loading `System.Management.Automation.dll`, CLR/assembly-load telemetry, and “telemetry gaps”).  

Technical Focus:
- PowerShell runspaces / custom hosting (`System.Management.Automation`)
- AMSI bypass via reflection (`AmsiUtils.amsiInitFailed`)
- ETW suppression via reflection (`EtwActivity.isEtwEnabled`)
- PowerShell Language Modes (FullLanguage vs ConstrainedLanguage)
- Detection opportunities: module/assembly load monitoring, CLR ETW, anomalous telemetry absence

Use Cases:
- Build a custom PowerShell host binary for authorized post-exploitation workflows
- Execute PowerShell tooling with reduced AMSI/ETW visibility inside a controlled runspace
- Validate blue-team detections for “PowerShell without powershell.exe” scenarios
- Hunt for suspicious processes loading `System.Management.Automation.dll` and reflection-based tampering patterns

Keywords:
PowerShell, Runspace, System.Management.Automation, AMSI, Antimalware Scan Interface, ETW, Event Tracing for Windows, Script Block Logging, AmsiUtils, amsiInitFailed, EtwActivity, isEtwEnabled, .NET Reflection, FullLanguage, Constrained Language Mode, WDAC, AppLocker, custom PowerShell host, telemetry evasion